    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize math instruction. They could break down tough concepts into smaller pieces, adapt to a student’s pace, and offer explanations in different styles. They could suggest interactive exercises and even identify where students are struggling. It could make learning more engaging and reduce anxiety by offering patient, consistent help."
